  Warnings:
  - Whole Building stitched 4 near-matching modular seam edge(s) within 0,0518 source
    units so fracture pieces can cross authored segment boundaries.
  - 'Shell breakdown (triangles, volume, watertight): #1 16 tri, vol 141,257, OPEN;
    #2 4 tri, vol 180,427, OPEN; #3 4 tri, vol 847,094, OPEN'
  - "Source has 3 separate mesh shells (0 closed, 3 found before preparation). Per-shell
    fracture: OFF (shells fracture merged) \u2014 classified as one hollow shell
    (an inner surface faces inward)."
  - Kept 6 nested surface islands together as one hollow shell. Auto Axis and every
    fracture plane are shared by the outer and inner walls so generated caps connect
    them instead of closing the cavity separately.
  - Fragment volume sum is 356% of the source volume. The source mesh is probably
    open or self-intersecting; caps were approximated.
  - Concrete fracture safely exported 242 of the configured maximum of 250. The remaining
    candidates would create an open boundary, an extreme needle or an invalid micro-fragment
    merge, so they were not exported.
  - 111 cut segment(s) could not be chained within the normal weld tolerance; affected
    caps preserved their real edge order and closed the final numerical seam.
  - Intact collision uses 3 compound convex parts because the source contains disconnected
    mesh islands.
  - 'Large Whole Building defers inactive fragment physics: only pieces that actually
    detach receive a Rigidbody. This keeps a local first break from registering all
    242 pieces with PhysX.'
